From 6ae8bdadc57139a55b02f9f35fe2b569be7e75cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: richard-rhino <richard-rhino@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 17:09:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Spec decode: fewer launches and no host sync in the Qwen4Exp
 MTP drafter

Two costs of each draft step on HPU:

- The draft model's glue around its decoder layer (input norms and projections, the
  stream reshape and the final stream mixer) was not part of any compiled region, so
  every op was a graph launch of its own for each draft token. Regional compilation
  now also compiles the methods and submodules a module names in
  `hpu_compile_regions`; the MTP predictor names its input projection and mixer, the
  Qwen4Exp model its final mixer (last PP rank).
- After the first draft pass the proposer read the target positions and the last
  token indices back from the device (a host sync before the next pass could be
  prepared). prepare_inputs keeps host copies of its indices, and the runner passes a
  host copy of the decode positions (DecodeInputData.position_ids_cpu); the device
  read stays as the fallback.

Unit test for the compile-regions hook.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
